Z||000000||speed racer||12-01-2001||05:26 PM||||I just got a new fiero and it has a 5-speed in it and was wanting a short shifter for it. I don’t want to spend the money to buy one could I have some one just cut it down and reweld it for me.<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||12-01-2001||05:36 PM||||I use a hack saw and cut a good 2" off the shaft and than drill and 1/8 inch hole at the bottem of the knob into the shaft and screw in a small screw, It will counter sink into knob, if you use the correct type of screw and only you will ever see it again.<P>Price for kit. $0.00 time to do &lt;1/2 hour.<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-02-2001||01:30 AM||||Funny you should ask.  I just made one tonight.  Since I recently purchased a 110v wire feed welder for my current project, I decided to make my own short shifter like others have described.  I took about 30 minutes and turned out really nice.  It is currently on ebay with a $25 buy it now price.  But since you don't want to spend money you could take yours to someone and have them cut it and reweld it.  It is easy to do, but keep in mind it takes the right tools to do these things, and they aren't cheap.  So, make sure you at least offer them a beer for their time and tools.||||reg||1
